  "summary": "Screened all 52 clients with the all-client views of client_updates, client_performance, drift_by_round, feature_summary and subgroup_outcomes (Sex, AgeGroup, Income), then confirmed with narrower queries. Three clients (IN, NE, WA) show a consistent free-rider signature: near-zero update norms in about half the rounds with random cosines, and normal training in the other rounds. Their local performance is normal, which rules out label noise and prevalence shift. Leads I did not report because they do not clear the noise-adjusted threshold: GU (largest drift mean shift, Stroke mean outlier, CITL z=-3.7, but n=708 and noise-adjusted z all below 3.5); VI and DC (drift shifts for small clients, not flagged after noise adjustment); DC's max_shift z=+3.9 (small client, no performance effect); CT GenHlth tail outlier (re-query at higher resolution showed no sentinel values); and AgeGroup/Income subgroup outliers (noise-adjusted z about 3-4, with over-recording rather than under-diagnosis). Budget is fully spent (0 remaining)."
